### Choideyy Contact API — VS Code REST Client
### Extension: humao.rest-client
### Set @baseUrl and @origin before running.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:5173

### Successful request
# @name success
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "subject": "General enquiry",
  "message": "Hello, I would like more information about Choideyy.",
  "formStartedAt": 1721400000000,
  "website": ""
}

### Missing required field (name)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "subject": "General enquiry",
  "message": "Hello, I would like more information about Choideyy."
}

### Invalid email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "subject": "General enquiry",
  "message": "Hello, I would like more information about Choideyy."
}

### Empty message
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "subject": "General enquiry",
  "message": ""
}

### Message exceeding maximum length (5001 chars)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "subject": "General enquiry",
  "message": "{{$repeat 5001 'M'}}"
}

### Invalid Content-Type
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: text/plain
Origin: {{origin}}

name=John&email=john@example.com

### Bot protection triggered (honeypot filled)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "subject": "General enquiry",
  "message": "Hello, I would like more information about Choideyy.",
  "website": "http://spam-bot.example"
}

### Bot protection triggered (submission too fast)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "subject": "General enquiry",
  "message": "Hello, I would like more information about Choideyy.",
  "formStartedAt": 9999999999999
}

### Rate limit exceeded
# Run this request 6+ times quickly from the same IP (limit is 5 / 15 min).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "subject": "Rate limit probe",
  "message": "Hello, this request is used to probe rate limiting behavior."
}

### CORS preflight
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Origin: {{origin}}
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type

### OpenAPI JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/openapi.json

### Swagger UI
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/docs

### Internal server error (mocked)
# This cannot be triggered via a normal client request without breaking SMTP.
# Covered by automated tests that mock sendContactEmail to throw.
# Expected response shape:
# HTTP/1.1 500
# { "success": false, "error": "Internal server error" }
